      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "An aviator with prolonged right sided low back pain is described. The diagnostic workup is presented leading to diagnosis of HLA B27 positive reactive sacroiliitis. Trial of sulfasalazine lead to resolution of his pain. The spondylarthropathies are briefly reviewed. Implications on his aeromedical status are discussed."},
